  "pass_a_gloss": "If you want to take the Scripture as a witness that sinners are punished even for the instruction of others, even if they at some time deny healing, hear Solomon speaking in the Proverbs: 'A fool being whipped — a cunning companion.' He did not say that the one being whipped becomes cunning and prudent through the blows, but that the fool is said to change from folly to prudence through the blows applied to the plague. For this is indicated by the name here of cunning. And the fool changes by seeing others whipped. Therefore it is beneficial for us, if we are to become worthy of salvation through others weeping, that others' punishment. And as the transgression of Israel was joined to the salvation of the nations, so the punishment of some will join to the salvation of others. Therefore, being good, God says: 'I will not spare, and I will not have compassion from their corruption.'",
